# Tables: a For style rule for a kind of table, with its Column sizes and its own cell rules inside.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Tables · A style for a kind of table
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: prices
			Column sizes: * 70 70
			Column align: left right right
			For element: Cell
				Box:
					Border: 0 0 0.5 0
					Border color: rule
			For element: Header cell
				Typography:
					Bold: true
					Color: accent
				Box:
					Border: 0 0 1.5 0
					Border color: accent
			For column: 3
				Typography:
					Bold: true
		For style: plain
			Column sizes: auto *
			For element: Cell
				Box:
					Padding: 1 12 1 0
	Section:
		Text: Tables
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: A style for a kind of table
		Paragraph: `Column sizes` and `Column align` can come from a rule, and the cell rules (`Header cell`, `For column`...) can go inside a `For style` rule. Then each table only says its `Style` and its rows.
			Style: intro
		Text: Style: prices
			Style: label
		Table:
			Style: prices
			Header rows:
				Row:
					Cell: Menu
					Cell: Lunch
					Cell: Dinner
			Body rows:
				Row:
					Cell: Daily menu
					Cell: 14.50
					Cell: 19.00
				Row:
					Cell: Tasting menu
					Cell: 38.00
					Cell: 45.00
		Text: Style: plain
			Style: label
		Table:
			Style: plain
			Body rows:
				Row:
					Cell: Opening hours
					Cell: Tuesday to Sunday, from 13:00 to 16:00 and from 20:00 to 23:00
				Row:
					Cell: Address
					Cell: 12 Main Square, Olot
